---
description: Rebase PR branches onto their latest remote base instead of merging the base branch
alwaysApply: false
---

# Rebase PR Branches

- When refreshing a PR, fetch current remote refs and rebase the PR branch onto
  the PR's declared remote base branch.
- Never merge the base branch into a PR branch.
- Before rebasing, confirm the local branch starts at the current remote PR head so no remote work is lost.
- After verification, update rewritten remote history only with an exact `--force-with-lease`.
- For stacked PRs, rebase bottom-up and preserve each PR's declared parent branch.
